    {
      "path": "src/ui/cockpit/replay/frame.tsx",
      "content": "Action cells are positioned by their array index, but the charts position each session using `s.plot.slot` (calculated from weekdays since the first date). If sessions have a gap—for example Monday followed by Wednesday—the Wednesday Action appears in Tuesday's column rather than under Wednesday's chart point. Preserve each session's plot slot in the cells and use that slot for grid placement; add an alignment case with non-consecutive session dates.",
      "existing_code": "      {actionKey \u0026\u0026 \u003cActionRow actionKey={actionKey} slots={plotBase.axis.slots} cells={sessions.slice(0, current + 1).map((s) =\u003e ({ dateLabel: s.dateLabel, ...(s.actionMark \u0026\u0026 { mark: s.actionMark }) }))} /\u003e}",
      "start_line": 118,
      "end_line": 118,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/cockpit/replay/action-row.tsx",
      "content": "Position cells using each session's plot slot rather than its array index. `plotSessionOf` counts weekdays and deliberately leaves holiday slots blank, whereas `i + 2` packs all sessions consecutively. After a weekday market holiday, every subsequent Action mark will therefore appear under an earlier chart date. Pass `session.plot.slot` into each cell and use `slot + 2` for its grid column; add a holiday-gap alignment test.",
      "existing_code": "          \u003cli key={dateLabel} style={{ gridColumn: i + 2 }} {...(!mark \u0026\u0026 { 'aria-hidden': true })}\u003e",
      "start_line": 11,
      "end_line": 11,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/cockpit/replay/day-words.props.ts",
      "content": "`heldQuantity` is the signed sum across instruments, so an open spread with one long and one short contract has a zero value even though both positions remain open. Such sessions fall through to “Nothing recorded.” (or fills only), losing both the missed-Review mark and the newest-session “Action: not chosen yet.” message. Check whether any individual position has a nonzero quantity instead, and add coverage for offsetting legs.",
      "existing_code": "  if (!session.heldQuantity.equals(ZERO) \u0026\u0026 (view.pending !== null || !newest)) {",
      "start_line": 34,
      "end_line": 34,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
